Artifact build
--------------

Data version:
  wikdict-2025.11.21+forms-2+cedict-2017.04.28+omw-2.0+unihan-17.0.0

SQLite SHA-256:
  3695295d07268725e555471217351c74e4f9375b8152974760fe12b926e1830e

Logical input/build fingerprint:
  dd843a0f60932951984c8167634f28a8c925e0390e93c6b93314ab6289378400

Builder:
  tools/build_dictionary.py (builder-v3; SQLite schema 1)

The builder verifies every source SHA-256 before parsing. It normalizes lookup
keys with Unicode NFKC plus case folding, creates read-only lookup indexes, and
retains source_id and provenance on every entry and every sense. It does not
add examples and never stems at query time. Builder v3 adds a small, reviewed
table of high-frequency English inflected-form index aliases from WikDict
headwords and explicit parts of speech. It deliberately does not apply generic
plural/tense rules to the whole lexicon. Ambiguous derived aliases are removed;
definitions remain unchanged and retain WikDict provenance. Meanings from
differently licensed sources remain separate rows with separate provenance.

